        &quot;progressBar&quot;: &quot;accent&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"visual"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"progressBar"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>accent<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">anonymizeDisplayedPaths</h3><a id="user-content-anonymizedisplayedpaths" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: anonymizeDisplayedPaths" href="#anonymizedisplayedpaths"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Replaces some known folder paths with their respective environment variable. Defaults to true.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;visual&quot;: {
        &quot;anonymizeDisplayedPaths&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"visual"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"anonymizeDisplayedPaths"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">enableSixels</h3><a id="user-content-enablesixels" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: enableSixels" href="#enablesixels"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Enables output of sixel images in certain contexts. Defaults to false.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;visual&quot;: {
        &quot;enableSixels&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"visual"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"enableSixels"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Install Behavior</h2><a id="user-content-install-behavior" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Install Behavior" href="#install-behavior"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>installBehavior</code> settings affect the default behavior of installing and upgrading (where applicable) packages.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Disable Install Notes</h3><a id="user-content-disable-install-notes" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Disable Install Notes" href="#disable-install-notes"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>disableInstallNotes</code> behavior affects whether installation notes are shown after a successful install. Defaults to <code>false</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;disableInstallNotes&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"disableInstallNotes"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Portable Package User Root</h3><a id="user-content-portable-package-user-root" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Portable Package User Root" href="#portable-package-user-root"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>portablePackageUserRoot</code> setting affects the default root directory where packages are installed to under <code>User</code> scope. This setting only applies to packages with the <code>portable</code> installer type. Defaults to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%/Microsoft/WinGet/Packages/</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note: This setting value must be an absolute path.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;portablePackageUserRoot&quot;: &quot;C:/Users/FooBar/Packages&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"portablePackageUserRoot"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>C:/Users/FooBar/Packages<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Portable Package Machine Root</h3><a id="user-content-portable-package-machine-root" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Portable Package Machine Root" href="#portable-package-machine-root"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>portablePackageMachineRoot</code> setting affects the default root directory where packages are installed to under <code>Machine</code> scope. This setting only applies to packages with the <code>portable</code> installer type. Defaults to <code>%PROGRAMFILES%/WinGet/Packages/</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note: This setting value must be an absolute path.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;portablePackageMachineRoot&quot;: &quot;C:/Program Files/Packages/Portable&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"portablePackageMachineRoot"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>C:/Program Files/Packages/Portable<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Skip Dependencies</h3><a id="user-content-skip-dependencies" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Skip Dependencies" href="#skip-dependencies"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The 'skipDependencies' behavior affects whether dependencies are installed for a given package. Defaults to 'false' if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;skipDependencies&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"skipDependencies"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Archive Extraction Method</h3><a id="user-content-archive-extraction-method" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Archive Extraction Method" href="#archive-extraction-method"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>archiveExtractionMethod</code> behavior affects how installer archives are extracted. Currently there are two supported values: <code>Tar</code> or <code>ShellApi</code>.
<code>Tar</code> indicates that the archive should be extracted using the tar executable ('tar.exe') while <code>shellApi</code> indicates using the Windows Shell API. Defaults to <code>shellApi</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;archiveExtractionMethod&quot;: &quot;tar&quot; | &quot;shellApi&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"archiveExtractionMethod"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>tar<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span> <span class="pl-ii">| "shellApi"</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Preferences and Requirements</h3><a id="user-content-preferences-and-requirements" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Preferences and Requirements" href="#preferences-and-requirements"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Some of the settings are duplicated under <code>preferences</code> and <code>requirements</code>. <code>preferences</code> affect how the various available options are sorted when choosing the one to act on.  For instance, the default scope of package installs is for the current user, but if that is not an option then a machine level installer will be chosen. <code>requirements</code> filter the options, potentially resulting in an empty list and a failure to install. In the previous example, a user scope requirement would result in no applicable installers and an error.</p>
<p dir="auto">When multiple values are listed under <code>requirements</code>, they are treated as an ordered preference in addition to a filter — the first listed value is preferred over subsequent ones when multiple valid options exist. If both <code>requirements</code> and <code>preferences</code> are set for the same field, the ordering from <code>preferences</code> takes precedence.</p>
<p dir="auto">Any arguments passed on the command line will effectively override the matching <code>requirement</code> setting for the duration of that command.</p>
<div class="markdown-alert markdown-alert-note" dir="auto"><p class="markdown-alert-title" dir="auto"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>These settings are only applied for the <code>winget install</code> command.</li>
<li>Other commands like <code>winget configure</code> are not affected by these settings.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Scope</h3><a id="user-content-scope" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Scope" href="#scope"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>scope</code> behavior affects the choice between installing a package for the current user or for the entire machine. The matching parameter is <code>--scope</code>, and uses the same values (<code>user</code> or <code>machine</code>).</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;preferences&quot;: {
            &quot;scope&quot;: &quot;user&quot;
        }
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"preferences"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"scope"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>user<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
        }
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Locale</h3><a id="user-content-locale" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Locale" href="#locale"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>locale</code> behavior affects the choice of installer based on installer locale. The matching parameter is <code>--locale</code>, and uses bcp47 language tag.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;preferences&quot;: {
            &quot;locale&quot;: [ &quot;en-US&quot;, &quot;fr-FR&quot; ]
        }
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"preferences"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"locale"</span>: [ <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>en-US<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>, <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>fr-FR<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span> ]
        }
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Architectures</h3><a id="user-content-architectures" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Architectures" href="#architectures"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>architectures</code> behavior affects what architectures will be selected when installing a package. The matching parameter is <code>--architecture</code>. Note that only architectures compatible with your system can be selected.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;preferences&quot;: {
            &quot;architectures&quot;: [&quot;x64&quot;, &quot;arm64&quot;]
        }
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"preferences"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"architectures"</span>: [<span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>x64<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>, <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>arm64<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>]
        }
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Installer Types</h3><a id="user-content-installer-types" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Installer Types" href="#installer-types"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>installerTypes</code> behavior affects what installer types will be selected when installing a package. It can also determine which type to install by default if a manifest has multiple types: The list is in priority order, with the first listed type being preferred over the others, and so on.  This is convenient for users who for instance prefer portable packages or MSIX/AppX installations. The matching parameter is <code>--installer-type</code>, which will override the settings.</p>
<p dir="auto">Allowed values as of version 1.12.470 include: <code>appx</code>, <code>burn</code>, <code>exe</code>, <code>font</code>, <code>inno</code>, <code>msi</code>, <code>msix</code>, <code>msstore</code>, <code>nullsoft</code>, <code>portable</code>, <code>wix</code>, <code>zip</code></p>
<p dir="auto">By default, when no user preference or requirement is configured, WinGet selects installer types in the following order: MSIX, MSI/Wix/Burn, Nullsoft/Inno/EXE, Portable.  If it is already installed, the same installer type will be required to ensure a proper upgrade.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;preferences&quot;: {
            &quot;installerTypes&quot;: [&quot;msi&quot;, &quot;msix&quot;]
        },
        &quot;requirements&quot;: {
            &quot;installerTypes&quot;: [&quot;msix&quot;, &quot;msi&quot;]
        }
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"preferences"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"installerTypes"</span>: [<span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>msi<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>, <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>msix<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>]
        },
        <span class="pl-ent">"requirements"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"installerTypes"</span>: [<span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>msix<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>, <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>msi<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>]
        }
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Default install root</h3><a id="user-content-default-install-root" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Default install root" href="#default-install-root"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>defaultInstallRoot</code> affects the install location when a package requires one. This can be overridden by the <code>--location</code> parameter. This setting is only used when a package manifest includes <code>InstallLocationRequired</code>, and the actual location is obtained by appending the package ID to the root.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;defaultInstallRoot&quot;: &quot;C:/installRoot&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"defaultInstallRoot"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>C:/installRoot<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Maximum resumes</h3><a id="user-content-maximum-resumes" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Maximum resumes" href="#maximum-resumes"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>maxResumes</code> setting determines the maximum number of times that a command may be resumed automatically. The default value is 3.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;installBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;maxResumes&quot;: 3
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"installBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"maxResumes"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">3</span>
    },</pre></div>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note: <a href="#resume">The resume behavior is an experimental feature.</a></p>
</blockquote>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Uninstall Behavior</h2><a id="user-content-uninstall-behavior" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Uninstall Behavior" href="#uninstall-behavior"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>uninstallBehavior</code> settings affect the default behavior of uninstalling (where applicable) packages.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Purge Portable Package</h3><a id="user-content-purge-portable-package" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Purge Portable Package" href="#purge-portable-package"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>purgePortablePackage</code> behavior affects the default behavior for uninstalling a portable package. If set to <code>true</code>, uninstall will remove all files and directories relevant to the <code>portable</code> package. This setting only applies to packages with the <code>portable</code> installer type. Defaults to <code>false</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;uninstallBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;purgePortablePackage&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"uninstallBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"purgePortablePackage"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Configure Behavior</h2><a id="user-content-configure-behavior" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Configure Behavior" href="#configure-behavior"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>configureBehavior</code> settings affect the default behavior of applying a configuration.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Default Module Root</h3><a id="user-content-default-module-root" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Default Module Root" href="#default-module-root"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>defaultModuleRoot</code> behavior affects the default root directory where modules are installed to. Defaults to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%/Microsoft/WinGet/Configuration/Modules</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note: This setting value must be an absolute path.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;configureBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;defaultModuleRoot&quot;: &quot;C:/Program Files/Modules/&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"configureBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"defaultModuleRoot"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>C:/Program Files/Modules/<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Download Behavior</h2><a id="user-content-download-behavior" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Download Behavior" href="#download-behavior"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>downloadBehavior</code> settings affect the default behavior of downloading packages.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Default Download Directory</h3><a id="user-content-default-download-directory" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Default Download Directory" href="#default-download-directory"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>defaultDownloadDirectory</code> setting affects the default directory where installers are downloaded to. Defaults to <code>%USERPROFILE%/Downloads/</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Note: This setting value must be an absolute path.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;downloadBehavior&quot;: {
        &quot;defaultDownloadDirectory&quot;: &quot;C:/Users/FooBar/Downloads&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"downloadBehavior"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"defaultDownloadDirectory"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>C:/Users/FooBar/Downloads<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Telemetry</h2><a id="user-content-telemetry" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Telemetry" href="#telemetry"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>telemetry</code> settings control whether winget writes ETW events that may be sent to Microsoft on a default installation of Windows.</p>
<p dir="auto">See <a href="/microsoft/winget-cli/blob/master/README.md#datatelemetry">details on telemetry</a>, and our <a href="/microsoft/winget-cli/blob/master/PRIVACY.md">primary privacy statement</a>.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">disable</h3><a id="user-content-disable" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: disable" href="#disable"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;telemetry&quot;: {
        &quot;disable&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"telemetry"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"disable"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">If set to true, the <code>telemetry.disable</code> setting will prevent any event from being written by the program.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Logging</h2><a id="user-content-logging" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Logging" href="#logging"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>logging</code> settings control the level of detail in log files.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">level</h3><a id="user-content-level" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: level" href="#level"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto"><code>--verbose-logs</code> will override this setting and always creates a verbose log.
Defaults to <code>info</code> if value is not set or is invalid.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;logging&quot;: {
        &quot;level&quot;: &quot;verbose&quot; | &quot;info&quot; | &quot;warning&quot; | &quot;error&quot; | &quot;critical&quot;
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"logging"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"level"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>verbose<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span> <span class="pl-ii">| "info" | "warning" | "error" | "critical"</span>
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">channels</h3><a id="user-content-channels" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: channels" href="#channels"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The valid values in this array are defined in the function <code>GetChannelFromName</code> in the <a href="/microsoft/winget-cli/blob/master/src/AppInstallerSharedLib/AppInstallerLogging.cpp">logging code</a>.  These align with the <em><strong>channel identifier</strong></em> found in the log files.  For example, <em><strong><code>CORE</code></strong></em> in:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="2023-12-06 19:17:07.988 [CORE] WinGet, version [1.7.0-preview], activity [{24A91EA8-46BE-47A1-B65C-CEBCE90B8675}]"><pre lang="plaintext" class="notranslate"><code>2023-12-06 19:17:07.988 [CORE] WinGet, version [1.7.0-preview], activity [{24A91EA8-46BE-47A1-B65C-CEBCE90B8675}]
</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">In addition, there are special values that cover multiple channels.  <code>default</code> is the default set of channels, while <code>all</code> is all of the channels.  Invalid values are ignored.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;logging&quot;: {
        &quot;channels&quot;: [&quot;default&quot;]
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"logging"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"channels"</span>: [<span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>default<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>]
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">fileNameStrategy</h3><a id="user-content-filenamestrategy" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: fileNameStrategy" href="#filenamestrategy"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Sets the default strategy for naming log files for installers that support it. <code>manifest</code> is the default and uses the manifest name. <code>timestamp</code> uses the date and time. <code>guid</code> uses a generated GUID. <code>shortguid</code> uses the first 8 characters of a generated GUID. Invalid values will revert to <code>manifest</code>.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="	&quot;logging&quot;: {
		&quot;fileNameStrategy&quot;: &quot;manifest&quot; | &quot;timestamp&quot; | &quot;guid&quot; | &quot;shortguid&quot;
	},"><pre>	<span class="pl-ent">"logging"</span>: {
		<span class="pl-ent">"fileNameStrategy"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>manifest<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span> <span class="pl-ii">| "timestamp" | "guid" | "shortguid"</span>
	},</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">file</h3><a id="user-content-file" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: file" href="#file"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>file</code> settings control the log files generated by winget during operation.  These settings apply to the automatic cleanup that happens whenever a Windows Package Manager process is run.
They only apply to the default log location, which contains winget logs, AppInstaller logs (the MSIX install UI), and is the default location where installer logs are placed.
The automatic cleanup happens at the beginning of the process, so the log file(s) generated by the current process will not be considered in the limits.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Setting</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Note</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>ageLimitInDays</code></td>
<td>The maximum age, in days, of files in the log directory; older files are deleted.</td>
<td>7 (days)</td>
<td>Set to 0 to disable this limit.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>totalSizeLimitInMB</code></td>
<td>The maximum size, in megabytes, of all files in the log directory; the oldest files are deleted first.</td>
<td>128 (MB)</td>
<td>Set to 0 to disable this limit.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>countLimit</code></td>
<td>The maximum number of files in the log directory; the oldest files are deleted first.</td>
<td>0</td>
<td>Set to 0 (the default) to disable this limit.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto">These settings apply to the log files that winget writes, only as they are being written.  They do not apply to files written by installers or the AppInstaller UI.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Setting</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Note</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>individualSizeLimitInMB</code></td>
<td>The maximum size, in megabytes, of an individual log file. If a file would exceed this limit, the logs will wrap. Note that this limit is approximate and the actual files may exceed it by a few bytes.</td>
<td>16 (MB)</td>
<td>Set to 0 to disable this limit.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;logging&quot;: {
        &quot;file&quot;: {
            &quot;ageLimitInDays&quot;: 7,
            &quot;totalSizeLimitInMB&quot;: 128,
            &quot;countLimit&quot;: 0,
            &quot;individualSizeLimitInMB&quot;: 16,
        }
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"logging"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"file"</span>: {
            <span class="pl-ent">"ageLimitInDays"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">7</span>,
            <span class="pl-ent">"totalSizeLimitInMB"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">128</span>,
            <span class="pl-ent">"countLimit"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">0</span>,
            <span class="pl-ent">"individualSizeLimitInMB"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">16</span>,
        }
    },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Network</h2><a id="user-content-network" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Network" href="#network"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>network</code> settings influence how winget uses the network to retrieve packages and metadata.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Downloader</h3><a id="user-content-downloader" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Downloader" href="#downloader"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>downloader</code> setting controls which code is used when downloading packages. The default is <code>default</code>, which may be any of the options based on our determination.
<code>wininet</code> uses the <a href="https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/win32/wininet/about-wininet" rel="nofollow">WinINet</a> APIs, while <code>do</code> uses the
<a href="https://support.microsoft.com/windows/delivery-optimization-in-windows-10-0656e53c-15f2-90de-a87a-a2172c94cf6d" rel="nofollow">Delivery Optimization</a> service.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <code>doProgressTimeoutInSeconds</code> setting updates the number of seconds to wait without progress before fallback. The default number of seconds is 60, minimum is 1 and the maximum is 600.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="   &quot;network&quot;: {
       &quot;downloader&quot;: &quot;do&quot;,
       &quot;doProgressTimeoutInSeconds&quot;: 60
   }"><pre>   <span class="pl-ent">"network"</span>: {
       <span class="pl-ent">"downloader"</span>: <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-pds">"</span>do<span class="pl-pds">"</span></span>,
       <span class="pl-ent">"doProgressTimeoutInSeconds"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">60</span>
   }</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Interactivity</h2><a id="user-content-interactivity" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Interactivity" href="#interactivity"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The <code>interactivity</code> settings control whether winget may show interactive prompts during execution. Note that this refers only to prompts shown by winget itself and not to those shown by package installers.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">disable</h3><a id="user-content-disable-1" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: disable" href="#disable-1"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="    &quot;interactivity&quot;: {
        &quot;disable&quot;: true
    },"><pre>    <span class="pl-ent">"interactivity"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"disable"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
    },</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">If set to true, the <code>interactivity.disable</code> setting will prevent any interactive prompt from being shown.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Experimental Features</h2><a id="user-content-experimental-features" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Experimental Features" href="#experimental-features"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">To allow work to be done and distributed to early adopters for feedback, settings can be used to enable "experimental" features.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <code>experimentalFeatures</code> settings involve the configuration of these "experimental" features. Individual features can be enabled under this node. The example below shows sample experimental features.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="   &quot;experimentalFeatures&quot;: {
       &quot;experimentalCmd&quot;: true,
       &quot;experimentalArg&quot;: false
   },"><pre>   <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalFeatures"</span>: {
       <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalCmd"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>,
       <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalArg"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">false</span>
   },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">directMSI</h3><a id="user-content-directmsi" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: directMSI" href="#directmsi"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">This feature enables the Windows Package Manager to directly install MSI packages with the MSI APIs rather than through msiexec.
Note that when silent installation is used this is already in affect, as MSI packages that require elevation will fail in that scenario without it.
You can enable the feature as shown below.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="   &quot;experimentalFeatures&quot;: {
       &quot;directMSI&quot;: true
   },"><pre>   <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalFeatures"</span>: {
       <span class="pl-ent">"directMSI"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
   },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">resume</h3><a id="user-content-resume" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: resume" href="#resume"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">This feature enables support for some commands to resume.
You can enable the feature as shown below.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="   &quot;experimentalFeatures&quot;: {
       &quot;resume&quot;: true
   },"><pre>   <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalFeatures"</span>: {
       <span class="pl-ent">"resume"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
   },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">fonts</h3><a id="user-content-fonts" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: fonts" href="#fonts"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">This feature enables support for fonts via <code>winget settings</code>. The <code>winget font list</code> command will list installed font families and the number of installed font faces.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="  &quot;experimentalFeatures&quot;: {
        &quot;fonts&quot;: true
  },"><pre>  <span class="pl-ent">"experimentalFeatures"</span>: {
        <span class="pl-ent">"fonts"</span>: <span class="pl-c1">true</span>
  },</pre></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">sourcePriority</h3><a id="user-content-sourcepriority" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: sourcePriority" href="#sourcepriority"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">This feature enables sources to have a priority value assigned. Sources with a higher priority will appear earlier in search results and will be selected for installing new packages when multiple sources have a matching package.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that search result ordering is dependent on several factors, and source priority is the lowest field in that currently (match quality and field are more important).</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="  &quot;experimentalFeatures&quot;: {
        &quot;sourcePriority&quot;: true
